From be7d3b0c2a8086a9e6c1884481b62dedbe91de2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:17:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Swarm audit 1ac5269f: renumbered nonce both ways, learned
 nonce, pasted routed speed-up, crediting note hashes, deploy target checks

Wallet (src/world/economyWallet.ts):
- Finding 1: the wallet's own hash under a lower nonce is accepted for a payment with this
  call's exact calldata or effect (one-time order id; the contract refuses a second payment).
  A lower-nonce revert, stake, withdrawal or approval stays refused (independent review).
- Finding 3: under a higher nonce the own hash is judged by the normal rules and ends as a
  replacement after finality instead of locked.
- Finding 2: learnNonce stores the higher nonce the wallet's pending copy of its own hash
  reports, so a speed-up or cancellation pasted later is checked against it. A tab holding
  the old nonce takes the stored intent over instead of judging (independent review).
- Finding 4: the intended effect is computed for every receipt; a pasted routed speed-up at
  the intent's nonce is confirmed after finality.
- Finding 6: state.paidOrder names the order of a confirmed payment (from its calldata).

Panel (src/world/WorldGoldPanel.tsx): marks both the sent and the judged hash mined
(finding 5); the order comes from paidOrder after a reload (finding 6).

Deploy (scripts/deploy.mjs): NODE_OPTIONS accepted only with a few harmless options
(finding 7); CLOUDFLARE_API_BASE_URL, CF_API_BASE_URL, CLOUDFLARE_COMPLIANCE_REGION,
WRANGLER_API_ENVIRONMENT and WRANGLER_CI_OVERRIDE_NAME refused, the account variable
recorded by name as manifest.targetEnv (finding 8); VITE_ matched with case everywhere
(finding 9).

Full suite 3,635 tests, 3,630 pass, 5 skipped (Windows symlink privilege), 0 fail.
17 mutations, each caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
